1
00:02:08,935 --> 00:02:10,362
<v Employer>Hello, is this John Murphy?


2
00:02:10,362 --> 00:02:11,728
<v Applicant>Hi, yes it is.


3
00:02:11,728 --> 00:02:19,958
<v Employer>Hi John, this is Ed Heisenburg from the Wild Dunes Spa and Resort calling about your application for our lifeguard position.


4
00:02:19,958 --> 00:02:22,073
<v Employer> Do you have a few minutes to talk?


5
00:02:22,073 --> 00:02:23,982
<v Applicant>Yes, absolutely

6
00:02:23,982 --> 00:02:25,729
<v Employer>Great. Could you give me your address?


7
00:02:25,729 --> 00:02:30,916
<v Applicant>Sure. My address is 45 Elsinore Court.

8
00:02:30,916 --> 00:02:33,738
<v Employer>I’m sorry, was that Eleanor? Could you spell that for me?


9
00:02:33,738 --> 00:02:39,550
<v Applicant>Sure - it’s Elsinore. E-L-S-I-N-O-R-E.


10
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:46,918
<v Employer>Okay, thanks. And is this the number we should reach you at in the future? 099885767?


11
00:02:46,918 --> 00:02:56,630
<v Applicant>No, this is my home phone, but let me give you my mobile phone number instead: 077896245. Call me on that one.


12
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:00,529
<v Employer>Okay - I’ll make a note of that. Could you tell me your availability?


13
00:03:00,529 --> 00:03:04,465
<v Applicant>Sure. I am usually available during afternoons or weekends.

14
00:03:04,465 --> 00:03:09,695
<v Applicant> I would prefer not to be scheduled on weeknights because I work part-time as a waiter.


15
00:03:09,695 --> 00:03:16,289
<v Employer>That shouldn’t be a problem, since we don’t stay open very late anyway. And do you have any other employment experience?


16
00:03:16,289 --> 00:03:23,852
<v Applicant>Yes, I have worked at a few other places. I was the baseball coach at Ridgemont High School last season.


17
00:03:23,852 --> 00:03:29,686
<v Employer>I see. And do you have any other experience that you would like us to note on your application?


18
00:03:29,686 --> 00:03:33,677
<v Applicant>Yes. Last year I worked at the beach as a rescue diver.


19
00:03:33,677 --> 00:03:36,072
<v Employer>Rescue diver? That sounds intense!


20
00:03:36,072 --> 00:03:45,394
<v Applicant>Well, it’s really just like being a lifeguard, except in the ocean instead of a pool. So kind if like being a lifeguard at the world’s largest pool.


21
00:03:45,394 --> 00:03:46,227
<v Employer>Haha. I see.


22
00:04:21,579 --> 00:04:27,017
<v Employer>So could you tell me about the relevant skills you have? I’m guessing a lot, given your experience.


23
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:31,007
<v Applicant>I am CPR certified and have 2 years of diving experience.


24
00:04:31,007 --> 00:04:38,360
<v Employer>Great! It sounds like you are well qualified for this position. When does your CPR certification expire?


25
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:47,541
<v Applicant>Hm. I think in November, but let me quickly check my CPR card… actually, it expires in October.


26
00:04:47,541 --> 00:04:53,295
<v Employer>Okay, so regardless you have it through the end of the summer. When is your ideal time to work?


27
00:04:53,389 --> 00:05:00,249
<v Applicant>Since I work in the restaurant on weeknights, I like weekends best - specifically Saturday mornings.


28
00:05:00,249 --> 00:05:08,846
<v Employer>I see. We do already have a lot of staff available on Saturdays, but I do need an early morning shift lifeguard.


29
00:05:08,846 --> 00:05:11,373
<v Employer> How early could you work Saturday morning?


30
00:05:11,373 --> 00:05:15,290
<v Applicant>I can get there by 6.00 if need be.


31
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:21,184
<v Employer>You’ll be happy to know we open a little later than that, but I’ll put you down for Saturday morning here.


32
00:05:21,184 --> 00:05:24,032
<v Applicant>Oh awesome! I can’t wait to get started.


33
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:27,487
<v Employer>How about you come in next Saturday, the 12th?


34
00:05:27,487 --> 00:05:28,467
<v Applicant>That sounds good.


35
00:05:28,467 --> 00:05:37,730
<v Employer>Great - We can figure out other shifts for you to work when you come in then. One last thing - just out of curiosity, where did you hear about us?


36
00:05:37,730 --> 00:05:41,515
<v Applicant>I heard your ad on the radio while I was driving this morning.


37
00:05:41,515 --> 00:05:46,420
<v Employer>You know, I think you’re the first person who has responded to our radio ads. 


38
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:49,641
<v Employer> It’s almost always people who have seen us in the newspaper.


39
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:53,162
<v Applicant>Yeah, I don’t have time to read through the newspaper every morning. 

40
00:05:53,162 --> 00:05:56,788
<v Applicant> I have plenty of time in the car to listen to radio ads.


41
00:05:56,788 --> 00:06:02,056
<v Employer>That makes sense. Well, thanks for your time, and we’ll look forward to seeing you on the 12th. 